{"c":[{"id":"a6b54378f08f606c","sum":"U2: Not right on an offer is a click on the slip's source row only (NotRightTarget); its keyboard path is the fact's row in What Caret knows. Off-screen stand-ins (ScrollingColumn) must take the height offered and clip, or the knows window's footer falls out of renders.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T000002Z-0878a22fa544c193","text":"U2: Not right on an offer is a click on the slip's source row only (NotRightTarget, a tiny click panel over that row); no key is claimed, and the keyboard path is the fact's row in What Caret knows.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T000002Z-0ab9ad748298511d","text":"U2: SwiftUI's off-screen stand-ins (ScrollingColumn) must take the height offered and clip, as a GeometryReader does; a fixed-size stack in a flexible frame pushed the knows window's footer out of renders.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"52b95150f4d0fe88","sum":"U2: debug JSON omits nil keys (read with .get()); the perch is a rim, perch and caption on the task's own window, drawn only while Rim.seen says it is uncovered; corner perch and perch-avoid are gone.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T000002Z-69ceb492909786b0","text":"U2: the host's debug JSON leaves out nil keys (synthesized Codable), so a script must read them with .get(); memory_documents_walk.py misread a closed editor as still open.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T000002Z-b1b1695c4d5b6282","text":"U2: the perch is now a rim, perch and caption on the task's own window, drawn only while Rim.seen says nothing covers it; the corner perch, PerchPlacement and perch-avoid are gone (perch-avoid now answers with an error).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
